<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<openrocket version="1.11" creator="OpenRocket 26.xx-SNAPSHOT-5f164fd0e">
  <rocket>
    <name>Simulation scripting</name>
    <id>b855b858-2833-4a1d-9078-79bd896038bb</id>
    <axialoffset method="absolute">0.0</axialoffset>
    <position type="absolute">0.0</position>
    <comment>This design demonstrates active roll control and air-start using simulation extension written in JavaScript.

The main fins are slightly misaligned, which causes roll to occur.

The fin set named CONTROL acts as a canard to control the rocket&#39;s roll.  The simulation listener checks the current roll rate during flight and applies a PID controller to control the angle of these fins, counter-acting the roll caused by the main fins.

You can see the applied script by opening a simulation and selecting Simulation options, then clicking the configuration icon of the simulation extension.

This is the first configuration of the Iso-Haisu hybrid rocket which was used to demonstrate active control of a rocket by the Finnish Astronautical Society.
-----------------------------------------------------------
Simulation #1 has no extensions added.
Simulation #2 has an active roll control script..
Simulation #3 has both active roll control and air-start scripts.</comment>
